# Line endings are decided here rather than by each contributor's core.autocrlf,
# so an editor that rewrites a file with the other convention cannot turn a
# one-line change into a whole-file diff.
#
# LF everywhere: that is what 57 of the 68 tracked files already used, and what
# every tool in this project (Python, git hooks, CI) reads without complaint.
# Windows handles LF fine; the exceptions that genuinely need CRLF are below.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Batch and PowerShell scripts: cmd.exe and older PowerShell hosts mis-parse a
# script that arrives with LF endings, so these are checked out with CRLF.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.ps1 text eol=crlf

# Never rewrite the bytes of these, and never try to diff them as text.
*.ico binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.gif binary
*.exe binary
*.dll binary
*.zip binary
*.whl binary
